      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "WU Jên-ch'ên 吳任臣 (T. 志伊, 爾器, 征鴻, H. 託園), 1628?–1689?, historian and mathematician, was a native of Jên-ho (Hangchow), Chekiang. Because of his achievements in the field of historical scholarship he was recommended in 1678 to take the special examination known as po-hsüeh hung-tz'ŭ (see under P'êng Sun-yü) which he passed in the ensuing year.",
